LA NOSTRA STORIA 
 Noi di ST crediamo nel potere della tecnologia di guidare l’innovazione e avere un impatto positivo sulle persone, sulle imprese e sulla società. Siamo un'azienda globale di semiconduttori e la nostra tecnologia avanzata e i nostri chip costituiscono la parte nascosta del mondo in cui viviamo oggi. 
 Entrando in ST farai parte di un'azienda di oltre 115 nazionalità e presente in 40 paesi, con oltre 50.000 creatori di tecnologia in tutto il mondo! 
 Lo sviluppo di tecnologie richiede più del solo talento: siamo infatti alla ricerca di persone straordinarie che comprendano la collaborazione e il rispetto. Persone con passione e il desiderio di rompere lo status quo, guidare l'innovazione e sbloccare il proprio potenziale. Intraprendi un viaggio con noi, dove puoi innovare per un futuro che vogliamo rendere più intelligente e più verde, in modo responsabile e sostenibile. La nostra tecnologia inizia con te.. 
 THE ROLE 
 The candidate will contribute to functional verification, software validation, and technical analysis activities for embedded components dedicated to the boot path, cryptographic cores, and related security mechanisms, with the goal of ensuring functional correctness, robustness of system behavior, and compliance with project requirements.
 The person will work closely with development, architecture, and validation teams, supporting the definition of test cases, execution of test campaigns, analysis of results, and debugging of potential anomalies on microcontroller targets and laboratory platforms.
 The candidate will therefore be responsible for:
 designing, implementing, and executing functional verification activities on embedded software/firmware;
 validating boot sequence flows, including aspects of secure boot , authentication, integrity checks, and startup controls;
 verifying the behavior of cryptographic cores and security support functionalities;
 developing test scripts and automation in Python and support components in C ;
 carrying out debugging activities on microcontrollers, analyzing registers, traces, signals, and execution states;
 using laboratory instrumentation such as oscilloscopes, logic analyzers, debug probes, and equivalent tools;
 collecting technical evidence and contributing to the traceability of bugs, issues, and nonconformities;
 supporting the preparation of validation reports, technical notes, and test documentation;
 interacting with cross-functional teams to clarify requirements, reproduce issues, and verify fixes;
 contributing to validation activities in compliance with the processes and constraints required by ISO 26262 .
 POSSIBLE EXTENSION TOWARD CYBERSECURITY 
 Over time, the scope of activities may also extend to embedded cybersecurity aspects, including for example:
 vulnerability analysis in startup flows and authentication processes;
 support for validation of secure boot , firmware protection, key management, and integrity protection mechanisms;
 verification of requirements related to hardening, trust chain, and resistance to software/hardware attacks;
 contribution to assessment activities on security functionalities and compliance with security by design requirements;
 collaboration in defining tests aimed at detecting anomalous behavior or tampering attempts;
 possible involvement in initiatives related to standards, best practices, or cybersecurity frameworks for embedded systems.
 REQUIRED SKILLS AND EXPERIENCE 
 Master’s degree in Electronic Engineering, Computer Engineering, Automation Engineering, Telecommunications, or related disciplines;
 Solid background in embedded systems, microcontroller architecture, firmware, and low-level debugging;
 Good knowledge of Python for test automation and data analysis;
 Good knowledge of C for understanding and analyzing software/firmware behavior;
 Experience using oscilloscopes, debug probes, logic analyzers, and laboratory instrumentation;
 Ability to perform technical debugging on embedded targets, also through analysis of signals, timing, and machine states;
 Familiarity with concepts such as secure boot, applied cryptography, firmware integrity, and trust chain;
 Knowledge of ISO 26262 and the related development, verification, and validation process in the context of safety-critical systems;
 Interest in, or preliminary knowledge of, embedded cybersecurity and hardware/software security topics;
 Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, attention to detail, and technical documentation capability;
 Excellent knowledge of English, both written and spoken.
 --------------------------------------------------------------------------
 IL RUOLO 
 Il candidato contribuirà alle attività di verifica funzionale, validazione software e analisi tecnica di componenti embedded dedicati al boot path , ai core crittografici e ai relativi meccanismi di sicurezza, con l’obiettivo di garantire correttezza funzionale, robustezza del comportamento del sistema e conformità ai requisiti di …

As an AI & Cloud Application Security Specialist, you will influence how cloud applications and AI-enabled solutions are assessed, secured and governed, turning complex security requirements into practical guidance that enables innovation while protecting our global business. 
 You will combine hands-on security assessments with consulting, governance, and cross-functional collaboration:
 Evaluate, review, and approve AI-enabled applications and SaaS solutions.
 Assess SaaS solutions, products, and architecture documentation for security risks, regulatory requirements, and compliance.
 Review AI and SaaS applications and features, provide security consulting, and contribute to the development of internal security guardrails, standards, and guidelines.
 Review security assessments and checklists, document outcomes, and approve solutions within delegated authority.
 Provide cybersecurity consulting to IT and business stakeholders, with a focus on AI, cloud, and SaaS-related initiatives.
 Support cybersecurity audits, testing activities, and security assessments, and help stakeholders remediate identified findings.
 Review, and support the definition and maintenance of cybersecurity rules, standards, guidelines, and checklists for AI and SaaS security, and advise stakeholders on their implementation.
 Drive the secure adoption of emerging AI and cloud technologies by balancing business enablement, innovation, risk management, and regulatory compliance, collaborating with architecture, legal, privacy, procurement, and business teams to ensure it.
Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Cybersecurity, Information Security, Computer Science, Information Technology, or a comparable qualification supported by relevant professional experience.
 At least five years of experience in enterprise IT, including a minimum of three years in cybersecurity, application security, cloud security, or a related field.
 Practical experience assessing applications, cloud services, SaaS solutions, architectures, and AI-enabled solutions for security risks and compliance requirements.
 Experience applying industry standards and frameworks such as OWASP, NIST, CIS Controls, ISO/IEC 27001, or comparable security frameworks.
 Solid understanding of cloud security concepts, web application security, identity and access management, authentication mechanisms, and encryption technologies.
 Knowledge of AI security concepts, AI governance, secure AI adoption, and risks associated with AI-enabled applications is highly desirable.
 Ability to analyze complex technical topics and translate security requirements into practical guidance for technical and non-technical stakeholders.
 Strong communication and consulting skills, with the ability to influence decisions and drive secure outcomes across international and cross-functional teams.
 Professional proficiency in English, min. B2.
 Relevant certifications such as CISSP, CCSP, CSSLP, Azure Security Engineer, AWS Security Specialty, or equivalent certifications are advantageous.
